     "title": "New Audio SoCs Combine Bluetooth HDT with Dual-RF Technology",
     "url": "https://semiwiki.com/ip/ceva/372013-new-audio-socs-combine-bluetooth-hdt-with-dual-rf-technology/",
     "time": "08-07 05:00",
     "ts": 1786050022,
     "summary": "Ceva and Actions Technology have expanded their longstanding partnership with the introduction of the ATS296X series, a new family of Bluetooth audio chips desi",
     "source": "SemiWiki",
     "content": "Ceva and Actions Technology have expanded their longstanding partnership with the introduction of the ATS296X series, a new family of Bluetooth audio chips designed to bring High Data Throughput technology into commercial wireless products. Powered by the Ceva-Waves Bluetooth HDT platform, the series is positioned as one of the industry’s earliest implementations of a capability expected to play a major role in the next generation of Bluetooth audio.\nBluetooth HDT is a key feature associated with the upcoming Bluetooth 7.0 specification. It raises peak data throughput from 2 Mbps to approximately 7.5 Mbps, creating more room for demanding applications that conventional Bluetooth connections cannot support as effectively. These include lossless multichannel audio, ultra-low-latency gaming sound, faster file transfers and substantially quicker over-the-air software updates.\nFor home entertainment, the added bandwidth could be especially significant. Earlier Bluetooth generations have generally limited native audio delivery to stereo. HDT can support more elaborate configurations, allowing soundbars to communicate wirelessly with satellite speakers and subwoofers. This could help manufacturers reduce cabling while offering richer, more flexible home theater systems.\nThe ATS296X series combines Actions Technology’s wireless audio SoC expertise with Ceva’s production-ready Bluetooth HDT intellectual property. By integrating the platform into a commercial chip family, Actions aims to give device makers a practical migration path to the emerging standard. Target products include Bluetooth speakers, wireless microphones, gaming accessories, multichannel home audio systems and other premium audio devices.\nThe collaboration also builds on a substantial shared history. Actions Technology has licensed Ceva’s audio DSP technology for its processing pipelines for years and has delivered more than 100 million wireless audio SoCs incorporating Ceva connectivity and sensing technologies. That experience provides an established foundation for moving HDT from specification work into manufacturable products.\nAccording to Ceva, its Ceva-Waves Bluetooth portfolio includes controller, modem, radio-frequency and software protocol stack IP. Before formal ratification of the next Bluetooth Core Specification, the company has taken part in four industry interoperability events, where it validated its HDT implementation with other major chipset providers. The ATS296X series is itself undergoing interoperability testing, an important step toward reliable operation across products from different vendors.\nActions Technology is also bringing its proprietary dual-RF design to the new series. The company says the architecture is intended to support concurrent operation across multiple scenarios, helping customers address a broader range of use cases. Combined with HDT bandwidth, the design is meant to deliver competitive wireless performance while simplifying development for manu",
     "_extract_method": "trafilatura",
     "zh": "新款音频系统级芯片融合蓝牙HDT与双射频技术",
     "content_zh": "Ceva与Actions Technology合作推出ATS296X系列蓝牙音频芯片，基于Ceva-Waves蓝牙HDT平台，是行业较早落地蓝牙HDT能力的商用产品。蓝牙HDT是蓝牙7.0规范核心特性之一，峰值数据传输速率从2Mbps提升至约7.5Mbps，可支持无损多声道音频、超低延迟游戏音效、更快文件传输及空中软件更新，还能让回音壁与卫星音箱、低音炮无线连接，适配家庭娱乐场景需求。"
