     "ts": 1786042800,
     "summary": "A little-noticed government policy shift caused a seven-year delay in choosing a costly medicine for Medicare price negotiations, an advocacy group says.",
     "source": "STAT News",
     "content": "A little-noticed policy shift by Medicare caused a seven-year delay in choosing a costly AbbVie medicine for price negotiations, a move likely to hurt taxpayers, according to an analysis by a consumer advocacy group.\nThe change occurred as the Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services readied a new round of talks with drugmakers over prices that the agency would pay for a limited number of medicines. The process was created by the Inflation Reduction Act, which became law in 2022 in response to the rising cost of prescription drugs.\nThis article is exclusive to STAT+ subscribers\nUnlock this article — plus in-depth analysis, newsletters, premium events, and news alerts.\nAlready have an account? Log in",
     "_extract_method": "trafilatura",
     "zh": "STAT+：倡导团体称Medicare让艾伯维爆款药物延迟7年才纳入价格谈判",
     "content_zh": "消费者权益倡导团体的分析显示，Medicare一项鲜少被关注的政策变动，导致一款昂贵的艾伯维爆款药物被纳入价格谈判的时间推迟了7年，这一举措很可能损害纳税人利益。此次变动发生在美国医保与医疗救助服务中心准备就一批有限数量药品的采购价格与药企开展新一轮谈判期间，该谈判流程由2022年出台的《通胀削减法案》设立，旨在应对不断上涨的处方药成本。"
